      "id": "EZS-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-exceptional-zero-saving",
      "title": "Fixed-modulus density and the multiplicity of each zero strip",
      "statement": "For the large-modulus explicit formula at T₀=m¹², let H=log(m(T₀+3)). The total multiplicity of the zeros in j<H(1−Re ρ)≤j+1 is bounded by 2C₁C exp(24(j+1))H¹¹. The logarithmic power from the local count accounts for close ordinates of the same character.",
      "hypotheses": "8 divides the positive integer m. The finite zero lists come from the smoothed explicit formula for characters modulo this fixed m, at heights |Im ρ|≤T₀+1 and 1−κ<Re ρ<1 with κ≤1/20. Its unit-height multiplicity bound and the separated-ordinate density theorem hold.",
